Design for Upgradability strategy aims to avoid the technological, psychological, or economical obsolescence of the product by facilitating the upgrade of components throughout various phases of the product or service life. This strategy should be planned during the architectural stage and can be performed by users, providers or original equipment manufacturers. It can be used by designers to enhance the bond between the product and its user (by changing the aesthetics of the product) or to restore the product to optimum working conditions (by changing the damaged component of the product). When the upgrade is performed by the user it is essential that the product is designed with standard and easy to find components.